# Installing cups is not the same as being able to print: the daemon is off
# until something enables it, and a printer plugged into a machine with cups
# installed but not running looks exactly like a printer that is not supported.
#
# The socket rather than the service on purpose - cups is socket-activated, so
# it starts on the first print job and is not running the rest of the time.
#
# Applied on the installed system by systemctl preset-all, which the installer
# runs at the end (see do_services in luna-install).
enable cups.socket
